+# tark_captions
+
+Tark's live captions engine (D4): the client's words on a call, computed on
+the Mac. Runs in the speech recognition utility process in place of SODA.
+
+- `ort_runtime.*` — ONNX Runtime, `dlopen()`ed from
+  `Tark.app/Contents/Frameworks/libonnxruntime.1.31.0.dylib` (the official
+  release, pinned in `downloads-onnxruntime.ini`); nothing links against it.
+
+Models (Phase 1: from `~/Library/Application Support/Tark/Captions/models/`,
+made by `utils/captions_export.py export`): AI4Bharat IndicConformer 600M
+(MIT; int8 encoder + CTC decoder), Silero VAD (MIT).
+
+`tark_captions_unittests` tests it without building the browser:
+
+```
+ninja -C out/Default tark_captions_unittests
+TARK_CAPTIONS_ORT=third_party/tark_onnxruntime/lib/libonnxruntime.1.31.0.dylib \
+TARK_CAPTIONS_MODELS=~/Library/Application\ Support/Tark/Captions/models \
+TARK_CAPTIONS_TESTDATA=<tarka-browser>/resources/captions/testdata \
+  out/Default/tark_captions_unittests
+```
+
+Tests that need a path skip when its variable is unset.
